  "texts": {
    "preamble": "R.Rengan vs / on 8 November, 2024 Author: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan Bench: G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.46 Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 08.11.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice G.K.Ilanthiraiyan W.P.(MD)No.4625 of 2018 and W.M.P.(MD)No.4706 & 4707 of 2018 R.Rengan ... Petitio /Vs./ 1.The Principal Chief Conservator of Forests And Chief Wildlife Warden, Panagal Maaligai, Saidapet, Chennai 600 015. 2.The Wildlife Warden, O/o. The Wildlife Warden, No.110, Public Office Road, Nagapattinam. ... Respond Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of Ind issue a Writ of Certiorarified Mandamus to call for the records per to the impugned order in Se.Mu.Aanai.No.VaVu1/26500/2016 dated 19.12.2016 passed by the 1st respondent and quash the same and consequently directing the respondents to issue necessary transport permission to the elephant as per rules and considering the schedul the temple festival during auspicious days. 1/6 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(M For Petitioner : Mr.R.Narayanan For Respondents : Mr.M.Senthil Ayyanar Special Government Pleader R.Rengan vs / on 8 November, 2024",
    "facts": "The petitioner owns elephant and he used to transport it for temple festivals during Hindu rituals. Therefore, the petitioner applied before the respondents seeking for permission to transport his elephant. However it was rejected on various grounds. They used to transport their elephants without giving enough rest to the elephants between functions and also without following the Tamil Nadu Captive Elephants (Management and Maintenance) Rules, 2011.",
    "arguments": ""
  },
